{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784302747,"nonce":"KD7ow8shK4PF7DB8e/otm3xjCUc=","title":"[dogfood][enhancement] support file/Secret-mounted GitHub App credential (bootstrap-free, GitOps)","message":"Today a GitHub App connection credential (the PEM) is stored in Postgres via PUT /v1/secrets at org _forge (ADR-0046). That has a bootstrap ordering problem for a k8s deploy: the server must be UP before you can store the credential it needs to authenticate, and the credential is lost whenever the DB is recreated (must re-PUT + re-register).\n\nMost GitHub-App services instead mount the PEM as a k8s Secret (file/env), available at boot and managed via GitOps. Proposal: let the forge adapter resolve the 'github-app' connection credential from a mounted file / env var (e.g. SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM_FILE) with the DB secret store as fallback, and expose it in the Helm chart (secrets.githubAppPem -\u003e mounted Secret). Keeps the API path for multi-tenant/runtime-managed creds, adds a boot-time path for the single first-party App.\n\nSurfaced during helm-based dogfood (in-cluster deploy, DB wiped between clean runs).","files":null}]}